Welcome to Unemployed OS — Arch under the hood, hired the moment you boot it.

This live session includes a GNOME desktop (Windows-style taskbar by
default; run `uos-layout-switcher <name>` for macOS/ChromeOS/Cinnamon/etc.
layouts), the Calamares installer, and Wine/creative-suite packages. See
the project README for what's install-verified vs. still boot-tested only.

For Wi-Fi, authenticate to the wireless network using the iwctl utility.
For mobile broadband (WWAN) modems, connect with the mmcli utility.
Ethernet, WLAN and WWAN interfaces using DHCP should work automatically.

After connecting to the internet, the Arch installation guide can be
accessed via the convenience script Installation_guide.
